L0: # MiniMax Agent Docs
L1: - [Welcome to MiniMax Code](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/welcome.md): MiniMax Code is a desktop AI Agent app for software development, everyday workflows, automation, and remote collaboration.
L2: - [Download and Install](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/get-started/download.md): Download MiniMax Code and install it on macOS or Windows.
L3: - [Create Your First Task](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/get-started/first-task.md): Start from the composer, attach context, and let MiniMax Code begin working.
L4: - [Coding and Work Modes](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/modes.md): Understand when to use Coding mode or Work mode in MiniMax Code.
L5: - [Workspace and Project Context](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/workspace.md): Attach a local project so the Agent can understand your files, scripts, and conventions.
L6: - [Tasks and History](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/tasks.md): Manage tasks, history, pinned items, and archived conversations in MiniMax Code.
L7: - [Conversation Collaboration](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/conversation-collaboration.md): Quote, comment on, and rate Agent replies directly in a conversation.
L8: - [Code Review](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/code-review.md): Use the built-in Review command to inspect local code changes.
L9: - [Permissions and Safety](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/workflows/permissions.md): Understand how MiniMax Code handles permission prompts for local files, commands, and external actions.
L10: - [Infinite Canvas](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/infinite-canvas.md): Bring your assets, ideas, and generated results onto one canvas, and create alongside your Agent.
L11: - [Goal](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/goal.md): Set a verifiable outcome for MiniMax Code and let it keep working until the goal is achieved or progress is blocked.
L12: - [Built-in Browser](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/browser.md): Open pages, preview generated HTML, and debug web work inside the MiniMax Code task view.
L13: - [Computer Use](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/computer-use.md): Let MiniMax Code operate apps on your computer directly for tasks that need a graphical interface.
L14: - [Files / Changes / Terminal Panels](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/panels.md): Use MiniMax Code panels to inspect files, code changes, and command output.
L15: - [Appearance](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/appearance.md): Adjust the display mode, theme, density, fonts, and colors of MiniMax Code.
L16: - [Shortcuts and Mini Window](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/shortcuts.md): Use global shortcuts, command palette, and the mini window to work faster.
L17: - [Updates and Feedback](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/desktop/updates-feedback.md): Check for MiniMax Code updates and submit feedback tickets from the desktop app.
L18: - [Agent Team](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/team.md): Use Agent Team for complex tasks that benefit from decomposition, collaboration, and verification.
L19: - [Custom Agents](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/custom-agents.md): Create dedicated Agents with their own role, instructions, skills, workspace, and channels.
L20: - [Custom Mini Apps](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/mini-apps.md): Bring information, tools, and everyday tasks together in one interface.
L21: - [MiniApp Overview](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/miniapp-overview.md): What MiniApp is, how it runs and is published, what is planned next, and two official examples: stocks and road trip planning.
L22: - [H3 Max Video Generation](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/h3-max.md): Create videos with sound from text prompts and reference media in MiniMax Code.
L23: - [Plugin Marketplace](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/plugins.md): Install and use domain plugins in MiniMax Code.
L24: - [Plugin Development and Submission Guide](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/plugin-submission.md): Capability choices, package layout, manifest fields, Skills and MCP servers, size limits, and the submission process for MiniMax Plugins.
L25: - [MCP Servers](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/mcp.md): Connect external tools and data sources to MiniMax Code.
L26: - [Memory](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/agents/memory.md): Let MiniMax Code retain useful preferences, project conventions, and long-term working patterns.
L27: - [Scheduled Tasks](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/automation/schedules.md): Let Agents run recurring work on a schedule.
L28: - [Remote Control](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/automation/remote-control.md): Connect to your desktop Agent from your phone to check progress, add instructions, and approve permissions.
L29: - [Messaging Integrations](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/automation/im.md): Collaborate with Agents through Telegram, WeChat, Lark, or Feishu depending on the locale.
L30: - [M Plan and Credits](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/account/usage.md): View your MiniMax Code subscription plan, credit balance, and usage quotas.
L31: - [MiniMax API Key](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/account/minimax-api.md): Configure your own MiniMax API key in MiniMax Code.
L32: - [Custom Models / BYOK](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/account/byok.md): Add a custom model provider with base URL, API key, API format, and model names.
L33: - [Configure BYOK Models with an Agent](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/account/byok-agent-setup.md): Configure custom models with an agent and verify real responses using curl on macOS and Windows.
L34: - [FAQ](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/help/faq.md): Frequently asked questions about MiniMax Code desktop.
L35: - [Feedback](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/code/help/feedback.md): Submit reproduction details, screenshots, and diagnostics when reporting issues.
L36: - [Quick Start](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/quick-start.md): Install MiniMax Code CLI, sign in, and complete your first terminal task.
L37: - [Features and configuration](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/features.md): Learn about MiniMax Code CLI entry points, interactive capabilities, configuration, and integrations.
L38: - [Workflows](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/workflows.md): Use MiniMax Code CLI for repository work, multi-turn tasks, plans, permissions, and session recovery.
L39: - [Configuration and models](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/configuration.md): Configure MiniMax Code CLI data directories, credentials, providers, models, proxies, skills, MCP, and plugins.
L40: - [Headless and CI](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/automation.md): Use mcode exec from Shell, CI, batch jobs, and evaluations with structured output and stable exit codes.
L41: - [ACP integration](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/integrations.md): Connect MiniMax Code CLI to editors and Agent hosts that support Agent Client Protocol.
L42: - [Command reference](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/reference.md): Review MiniMax Code CLI top-level commands, options, and machine-readable output entry points.
L43: - [Security and permissions](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/security.md): Understand MiniMax Code CLI permission modes, credential protection, and automation boundaries.
L44: - [Troubleshooting](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/cli/faq.md): Troubleshoot MiniMax Code CLI installation, sign-in, configuration, automation, and terminal issues.
L45: - [Changelog](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/changelog.md): Track every update to MiniMax Code.
L46: - [Tech Blog](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/techblog.md): Technical articles from the MiniMax Agent engineering team.
L47: - [Common Issues](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/question.md): Solutions for common MiniMax Code client startup, login, unresponsive app, and log upload issues.
L48: - [Building a Testbed for Coding Agents](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/techblog/coding-agent-eval.md): Starting from MiniMax Code, building an evaluation system that can tell whether a Harness change actually helps.
L49: - [I stopped babysitting my coding agents. Here's the workflow.](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/techblog/coding-agent-workflow-and-skills.md): What an audit of my multi-agent setup changed, and how I now define, verify and deliver work with core-grill, core-spec and deliver.
L50: - [MiniMax Code Is Open Source: Inside the Harness Behind a Coding Agent](https://agent.minimax.io/docs/techblog/minimax-code-harness.md): Following one task through MiniMax Code: how each turn's capabilities are assembled, how context is managed, how tools are executed, how history is committed, and how sub-agent results are confirmed.
L51: ## AsyncAPI Specs
L52: 
L53: - [asyncapi](/docs/api-reference/speech/t2a/api/asyncapi.json)

